ent-SensorRadarCiv = AN/SP-300
    .desc = A generic navigation radar for civilian ships. Low power draw, but poor range. Can't provide a targeting solution for weapons.
    .suffix = Generic/Civ, T1, active radar, search only

ent-SensorRadarCivT2 = AN/SP-650
    .desc = A low-grade search & FCR radar for civilian ships. Good range, poor chaff resistance.
    .suffix = Generic/Civ, T2, active radar, search & FCR

ent-SensorRadarPdvOrekh = KOLS-4 Orekh
    .desc = A perfect little search radar. Manufactured in the USSP.
    .suffix = PDV/USSP, search radar

ent-SensorRadarPdvFCR = SN/5-K1 FCR
    .desc = An FCR manufactured in the USSP. Can only provide directional search functionality, but can serve as a low-cost solution to provide fire control capabilities to supplement KOLS-4.
    .suffix = PDV/USSP, FCR

ent-SensorRadarPdvFregat = KOLS-8 Fregat-PMM
    .desc = A high-powered basic search radar design for light ships. Manufactured in the USSP. Low power draw, no FCR. Very sensitive to both ships & chaff.
    .suffix = PDV/USSP, search radar

ent-SensorRadarPdvKara = KOLS-23 Kara
    .desc = A large AESA radar kit operated primarily by the PDV & USSP. Practically perfect - if you can handle the thermal signature and power draw.
    .suffix = PDV/USSP, search & FCR

ent-SensorRadarPdvMainstay = P-300 Mainstay
    .desc = An extremely high-powered AESA radar for PDV & USSP vessels. Can practically detect the entire sector, but has an insane power draw.
    .suffix = PDV/USSP, search & FCR

ent-SensorRadarTsfXiaoDou = Type-860 XiaoDou
    .desc = A basic radar kit outfitted on most TSF vessels. Provides a combined FCR & search capability, with decent resistance to chaff, but poor range.
    .suffix = TSF/CSec, search & FCR

ent-SensorRadarTsfRenHai = Type-890 RenHai
    .desc = A more advanced radar kit outfitted on most TSF vessels. Developed from the Type-860 - provides more sensitivity, but has a higher power draw & chaff resistance.
    .suffix = TSF/CSec, search & FCR

ent-SensorRadarTsfLiuDou = Type-445 LiuDou
    .desc = A large radar kit outfitted on most mid-sized TSF vessels. Very good, but very high power draw.
    .suffix = TSF/CSec, search & FCR

ent-SensorRadarTsfSanDian = Type-550 SanDian
    .desc = A large AESA radar kit operated primarily by the TSF. Practically perfect - if you can handle the thermal signature and power draw.
    .suffix = TSF/CSec, search & FCR

ent-SensorRadarTsfBeiDou = Type-940 BeiDou
    .desc = An extremely high-powered AESA radar for TSF vessels. Can practically detect the entire sector, but has an insane power draw.
    .suffix = TSF/CSec, search & FCR

ent-SensorInfraredTSF = Yu-5K11
    .desc = An IRST module commonly found on TSFN/TSFMC ships. Capable of identifying range, and bearing of thermal signatures.
    .suffix = TSF, infrared

ent-SensorInfraredPDV = STYX
    .desc = An IRST module produced and exported in absurd amounts by USSP manufacturers, and used by both the PDV and USSP for their ships. Capable of identifying range, and bearing of thermal signatures.
    .suffix = PDV/USSP, infrared

ent-SensorInfraredCiv = AN/AAA-9
    .desc = An IRST module produced by basically everyone. Capable of identifying range, and bearing of thermal signatures.
    .suffix = Generic/Civ, infrared

ent-SensorPassiveRadarTSF = DianCi-492
    .desc = The standard EM suite used across TSFN & TSFMC ships. Capable of identifying range, bearing, and output of detectable active radars.
    .suffix = TSF, passive radar

ent-SensorPassiveRadarPDV = SPO-63/AK-M
    .desc = An EM suite produced and exported in absurd amounts by USSP manufacturers, and used by both the PDV and USSP for their ships. Capable of identifying range, bearing, and output of detectable active radars.
    .suffix = PDV/USSP, passive radar

ent-SensorPassiveRadarCiv = AN/Sp-39
    .desc = An EM suite produced by basically everyone. Capable of identifying range, bearing, and output of detectable active radars.
    .suffix = Generic/Civ, passive radar
